WEBVTT

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:05.630
We've only got a week left until the prelims start.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.460
But nothing we can do right now.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.500
Why don't we just practice in the hallway again?

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.380
We got in trouble for that last time. They bitched at us for
all the squeaky noise our shoes were making.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.590
Doesn't this school have a training room or something?

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:19.670
Kuzu High isn't some prestigious school
with fancy shit like that.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.750
We wait until either the volleyball team
finishes using the court.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.840
Or the rain lets up.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.750
What a waste of a precious Saturday.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:30.460
Okay!

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.460
Memorize these!

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.380
Uh, let's see, Nanao has a 4.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.040
Yasuhara has an 11, no wait, a 14 I think?

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.960
And, uh, Chucky has a...

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.500
A woman.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:43.420
Wow.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:46.040
How on Earth could you know that
when your back is facing us?!

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.790
It's gotta be a trick of some kind, I just know it!

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:51.090
You always fail 'cuz you try
to memorize them one-by-one.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:54.920
You'll never be a good point guard
unless you learn to look at the bigger picture.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:59.630
Just imagine you had to pick
your favorite girl out of 100 of them,

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:02.250
you gotta be able to decide at just a glance
or they won't be impressed.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:06.290
You don't have to worry about that happening,
because it's a complete fantasy!

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:10.090
Besides, I'm not a horse. I don't have monocular vision
that lets me see both front and back!

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:12.840
Dude, did you seriously just compare me to a horse?

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.540
Brace yourself for my patented Rock Chop later!

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:16.750
"Patented"? That's just a plain old punch, man.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:19.920
But damn, the rain just won't let up today.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:23.540
That's fine by me.
We need a break from practice sometimes.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:27.000
I guess this is the best a regular high school can offer.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.420
Does this team really stand any chance... at winning?

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.090
Um, hey.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:35.460
Huh?

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.630
We're going to wrap up our practice for today.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:39.420
Here are the keys for the gym.

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:42.920
Are you sure? You've only been using it
for about an hour...

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:44.880
The rain ruined everything.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.790
Most of our members didn't even show up.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:48.630
And we've got midterm tests next week, anyway.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.630
The badminton team also started packing up early.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.290
I guess we do get lucky sometimes!

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:58.340
This means we can use the whole court all we want!

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:02.710
Uh, that's great, but shouldn't some of you
be studying for the upcoming tests, too?

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:04.540
Ain't nothing to worry about!

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.790
Oh really? I guess you guys must be pretty smart, then.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:09.630
Haha! That's a laugh!

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:11.920
I'm gonna bomb all the tests just like I always do!

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:14.130
That's not something to be proud of!

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:22.340
It's Shigeyoshi...

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:31.420
Kagami ni senaka mukete ayumu hodo ni toozakaru yume yo 
Back to the mirror, my dream getting farther with every step I take

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:35.880
Massugu kimi to mukiaitai 
I want to come face-to-face with you

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:42.500
Dekinai jibun e to "never mind" 
Saying to the incapable version of myself, "never mind"

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:50.020
Ahiru no Sora

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:56.340
Nagare sagyou de waketeyuku yume 
A dream slowly dismantled on the assembly line

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.630
Muki? Fumuki? Iwaba rongai? 
(Suitable? Unsuitable? Pretty much impossible?)

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:04.040
Koe mo naku kietetta koe 
True feelings gone missing without a whisper

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:07.040
Tameiki sura denai 
(Not even capable of a sigh)

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:13.250
Hito no sei ni shitatte owarenai 
None of it will end by placing the blame on others

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:17.210
Me no mae ni kiritatta ima 
Right now, in the face of a steep slope

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:21.250
"Koetai" to kokoro ga sakenderu 
My heart cries out for me to "overcome it"

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:28.790
Dekinai wake o sagasu nara daredemo dekiru sa 
Finding excuses not to try is something that anybody can do

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:36.340
Agaki hashitta sono saki mada shiranai jibun to deau 
Pushing myself to run beyond, I went to meet a me I've never known

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:42.710
Kabe ni kizamikonda rakugaki to "never mind" 
There's graffiti etched on the wall that says "never mind"

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:46.790
Ima asu e to hazume 
Now, I bounce into tomorrow

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:57.750
Light

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:57.590
Nobody was here, so I thought you canceled practice.

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:58.710
Ah, no.

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.710
We take turns using the gym with the other teams.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:02.500
Lemme help you out!

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:03.960
Uh, thank you.

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:06.380
We have free reign of the gym for once.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:08.000
Let's lower the glass boards in the middle.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:11.340
Sure, we'll rock-paper-scissors
for who does the hard work. Here we go!

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:14.590
Rock, paper, scissors...!

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:14.590
Shoot!

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:17.340
Please allow me to join the basketball team.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:24.670
I would like to apologize for lying to all of you.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:26.590
Shigeyoshi...

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:28.880
I'm sorry. Please forgive me.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.210
But, the truth is...

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:34.670
...I want to get serious about playing basketball again.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.290
Please let me join.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:38.920
Hold up.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:43.130
We've already seen your true colors.
You can't expect to just smooth talk your way in now.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:44.290
Kite.

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:48.340
Despite how our team looks,
we're working really damn hard to reach the top.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:52.210
Your half-assed passion for the game
is just gonna drag us down.

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:53.540
Go back to playing chemist, fool.

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:56.420
Hey! Be nice, Natsume!
You don't have to act so rude all the-

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.840
We're wasting precious time. Let's get to practicing.

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:00.420
R-right...

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:10.250
The reason I came here...
is because I have true passion for the game.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:16.670
I'm serious. I want to play basketball.

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:20.540
But what about the chemistry club?

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:24.840
I just finished turning in
my formal resignation to the club advisor.

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:28.000
There's nowhere else for me to go now.

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:29.710
Please allow me to stay with you.

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:31.040
You're not an orphan, jeez.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:34.750
Since he's this insistent about it,
I don't see any reason to say no.

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:36.420
It's just fine by me, personally.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:39.250
I don't agree.

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:41.670
Kurumatani...

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:45.590
I can't bring myself to believe him
when he claims to be "serious."

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:48.920
Color me surprised.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:51.000
Tinytown is totally picking a fight, guys.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.170
Then how can I convince you?

00:05:56.920 --> 00:05:58.040
Come out on the court.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:00.500
Is this for real?

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:05.420
Okay. I get it.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:10.840
He's fast!

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:15.380
Whoa! A double frappé!

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:17.130
It's a double clutch, dude.

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:20.250
That's one basket for me.

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:27.630
I see... blocks are inevitable for him,
so his playstyle is all about dealing with them.

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:31.710
This is like watching an adult play a kid.

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:36.210
It doesn't matter how good Kurumatani is on the court,
he won't be able to stop Shigeyoshi's shots.

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:38.250
There's just too much of a gap in height.

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:40.960
It doesn't matter.
Their skills will be what decide this match.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:46.880
Whoa, that was a smooth move!

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:51.710
And now, we're even.

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:57.380
Is it just me, or is Kurumatani acting
a little strange today?

00:06:57.670 --> 00:07:00.630
He was the one most excited about the idea
of Shigeyoshi joining us.

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:04.840
Did he just get really upset at being lied to, or what?

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:12.630
You should be... guarding me more closely.

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:13.380
Huh?

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:21.590
I'm not missing a single shot today.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.960
He scored from long-range on me in a one-on-one...

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:28.170
Dammit!

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:32.540
There it is!

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:44.040
What's the matter?

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:45.840
We've barely been at it for 10 minutes.

00:07:47.130 --> 00:07:48.880
Is this really how you play when you're "serious"?

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:52.290
A'ight! That's enough!

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:55.290
We can't waste any more time.
Get ready to start practice!

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:58.960
Hey! I think this guy is at his limit already.

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:00.710
What? No...

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:02.290
Hit the bench and rest up.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:03.540
But I...

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:04.540
You're in the way!

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:06.500
Sekiya! Sub out with him!

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:08.420
Hold it right there!

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:09.670
Ow!

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:11.500
Whoa! The girls are invading our turf!

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:13.540
Why are you guys bullying the new guy like that?

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:17.000
Don't the freshman have
their own training schedule to follow?

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.000
Jerks.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.380
Yeah, well, this guy doesn't even look like a freshman.

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:23.670
Speak up for yourself when you need a break.

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:27.750
Don't let anybody else determine what your limits are.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:30.000
Senpai...

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:35.420
I'm not done yet.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:39.170
I can still keep playing.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:55.210
Oh my gosh... that was high enough to be a dunk!

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.340
And now, we're even once again.

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:00.880
That was definitely a foul. Just now.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:04.630
No way, that's typical contact for under the basket.

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:10.920
They've been at it for 30 minutes already.

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:13.630
That Mokichi guy is pretty decent for hanging on so long.

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:14.290
Yeah.

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:16.880
He's just trying to skip out on actual practice.

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:19.630
I knew a guy like that back in middle school.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:23.500
It definitely doesn't seem that way to me, though.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:23.960
Huh?

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:27.210
That guy has gone... well beyond his limit.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:30.750
A crossover!

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:48.340
Not yet. Let's keep going.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:58.460
I'm sick and tired... of shouldering people's expectations.

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:02.880
And I'm already used...
to people being disappointed in me.

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:07.880
But... the truth is...

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:10.090
none of that ever really mattered to me at all.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:17.920
All of the seniors... on the day
of our very last tournament together...

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:21.960
I've gotta block!

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.480
Saijo

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.480
Kozu

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:15.500
Tsukishima...

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:19.670
What I feared more than anything...

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:22.790
was losing the light you brought.

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:36.420
Holy shit, check that dunk! Badass!

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:40.840
He plays pretty rough despite looking so timid.

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:42.210
He's showing off too damn much.

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:47.710
Looks like... I win.

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:49.290
He just smiled!

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:51.040
I didn't think that was possible for him!

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:52.960
What the hell gave you that impression?

00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:54.670
Shigeyoshi...

00:11:56.210 --> 00:11:57.250
Smug jerk...

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:01.000
I looked up the word "regret"...

00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:06.210
...in the dictionary.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:11.630
I realized... I was an idiot.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:14.040
See ya.

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:14.960
Bye.

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:26.920
Wait, isn't this your friend, Kyoko?

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:28.960
How terrible, don't you have an umbrella?

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:33.500
I forgot mine... back at school.

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:35.290
Even though it's raining so hard?

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:36.880
Quick, find a towel!

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:44.250
The truth is... that I did like you back then, Tsukishima.

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:48.130
Yeah. I know.

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:51.210
And... I still do now.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:55.000
I know that, too.

00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:02.880
Goodbye.

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:04.710
Wait, Kyoko!

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:06.040
What's with you?

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:09.170
I don't know what's going on,
but you're being way too hard on him.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:12.420
You should at least listen to what he has to say.

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:18.340
Senpai... I've decided
to start playing basketball once again.

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:23.460
If things go well, my team will go up against
the one from your school in the second round.

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:28.340
A huge mistake... that I'll never be able to undo.

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:32.880
That is the burden... which I must live with.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:42.000
That was so mean of you, Kurumatani.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:45.590
Shigeyoshi actually came to us
without needing any convincing.

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:48.290
Don't you want to play on the same team with him?

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:54.790
I think... there really are people in the world
too sick to play basketball even though they want to.

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:59.790
That's why... it was impossible for me
to just forgive Mokichi for lying about that.

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:02.500
Kurumatani...

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:03.380
But...

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:06.590
...I'm glad it wasn't true.

00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:12.290
In the end, I still really do want to play basketball...
together with Mokichi.

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:17.250
We have a new member I need to introduce to you.

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.460
Or at least, I wanted to, but...

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:23.340
...he's apparently out sick with a cold today.

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:25.420
You gotta be kidding!

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:28.210
So now, I'll just skip to today's announcements.

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:31.960
As you all know, the midterm tests will begin tomorrow.

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:35.880
Generally speaking, all teams are on break
during the testing period...

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:36.920
What?!

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:38.790
Wha-?! Hold on a damn second!

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:41.460
We only have 6 days left until the prelims start!

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:44.000
And I still haven't been able to get my shots to go in!

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:47.040
If we stop practicing this week then we're doomed!

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:48.130
Ban the tests instead!

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:51.630
I'm fully aware. Relax, I'm not a complete tyrant.

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:54.590
For the following four days that the tests are being held...

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:58.090
...you boys are free to make use
of the empty gym in whatever way you see fit.

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:00.630
Oh sweet, that's an awesome deal.

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:01.840
This is perfect.

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:04.250
Especially since school gets out at noon
during test week!

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.250
It'll be like a mini training camp!

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:08.880
That means we'll be able to pack our schedule totally full.

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:09.750
For sure!

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:13.340
Midterms! For the win! Yes!

00:15:13.340 --> 00:15:14.920
Uh, just one more thing.

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:20.420
If any of you end up with a failing grade
on the midterm tests, I'll pull you from the prelims.

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:23.750
Seriously...?

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:24.880
Dead serious.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:27.880
WHAAAAT?!

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:30.420
Okay, that's a big problem.

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:33.210
For now, just raise your hand if you expect to fail a test.

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:34.340
Okay!

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:36.790
That's basically the entire team!

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:39.790
What about that Mokichi guy who just joined?

00:15:39.790 --> 00:15:42.420
Maybe we can drop him before he ruins it for us.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:44.670
Worry about yourselves first!

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:49.130
Shigeyoshi went to THE Saijo Middle School,
so he must be plenty smart and talented!

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:49.880
For real?!

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:51.790
Jeez, what a damn glory hound!

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:57.540
Anyways, I think our best bet is to focus on just
the key subjects and study in groups split by grade.

00:15:58.290 --> 00:15:59.710
What tests are tomorrow?

00:15:59.710 --> 00:16:02.500
Do you all know what to expect?
Have you been taking notes in class?

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:03.840
Nope.

00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:04.630
Beats me.

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:05.670
Who uses notebooks?

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:08.460
You can memorize info by eating textbooks, you know.

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:11.380
P-please give me a few pages!
I'll top them with some mayo!

00:16:11.920 --> 00:16:16.630
So hey, "Kings of the Animal Jungle" is on tonight.
Can I go home early?

00:16:16.630 --> 00:16:19.460
Okay, I've had it up to HERE with you guys!

00:16:19.710 --> 00:16:23.630
Starting right now, NOBODY can leave the gym
without my express permission!

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:24.840
HUH?!

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:27.290
First Semester Midterm Schedule

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:27.290
Day 4

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:27.290
Day 3

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:27.290
Day 2

